## Why this is the task that fixes the reported bug

`show.rs:204` dispatches Rich mode to `IssuePanel` and everything else to the
compact `format_issue_details`. This is the terminal-facing path, so this is
where `br show` starts rendering markdown.

The compact path stays exactly as it is — piped output, `--no-color` and
`--json` keep byte-identical raw markdown.

## Ordering constraint — do not get this backwards

`sanitize_terminal_text` runs on the **source**, before `render_markdown_text`.
The renderer's own escapes are then the only ANSI present, and a crafted
description cannot inject its own.

Reversing the order would strip the escapes just generated *and* pass source
escapes straight through — a terminal-injection hole. Step 1's second test is
what pins it.

